// Code generated by forge. DO NOT EDIT.
// forge-owned: regenerated every run — do not edit (forge project disown to take ownership)
// Source: proto/services + each service's Deps struct.
//
// The EXPLICIT per-service mount surface. Two surfaces, one construction (the
// *Components bag from compose.go):
//
//   - TYPED MOUNTS — the run path. Each service has a typed method
//     `(*Components).Mount<Svc>(mux, opts...) []string` that mounts EXACTLY
//     that service over the constructed *Components and returns its Connect
//     path. The cli layer hands one of these METHOD VALUES to Serve —
//     selection is compile-time typed, never a string lookup. To run a single
//     service, its typed subcommand names the Mount<Svc> method DIRECTLY; there
//     is no name->func map.
//
//   - DATA-ONLY INVENTORY — introspection ONLY. `Inventory` is a pure
//     descriptor (names, connect-paths, kind, version) that `forge project map` /
//     `forge project audit` and the `services` listing read. It carries NO mount
//     closure and is NEVER on the run path. Names here are for DISPLAY.
//
// Construction lives entirely in compose.go (NewComponents). Names are never a
// construction key.
//
// PER-SERVICE OPTIONS. MountOptions has one field per service: the
// mountkit.Options that service's mount gets on top of the shared chain —
// mountkit.WithInterceptorsV2(...) (run AFTER the shared chain, so the shared
// interceptors wrap them; the service then gets a connect.Server of its own on
// the same mux), mountkit.WithHTTPOptionsV2(...) and/or
// mountkit.WithHTTPStack(...). The zero value is none. Owned code builds the
// value and names one of its methods as the mount; each is a MountFunc:
//
//	Mount: app.MountOptions{Worktree: []mountkit.Option{mountkit.WithInterceptorsV2(wake)}}.MountAll
//	Mount: app.MountOptions{Worktree: ...}.MountWorktree // a per-service subcommand
//
// (*Components).Mount<Svc> and MountAll are the same mounts with no options.
// For a change beyond that (a carved cross-edge),
// `forge project disown internal/app/mounts_services_gen.go` and own the bytes.
